    "original_source": "E. Chatelain, La tachygraphie latine des manuscrits de Verone, in Revue des Bibliothèques, XV, 1905",
    "description": "Handwritten reproduction of Chatelain's complete sign list from Veronese manuscripts. Each entry maps a sign to a syllable value with manuscript line-number references. This represents the codex-scribal tradition (literary manuscripts) as opposed to Costamagna's notarial tradition (legal documents).",
    "notes": "The two handwritten pages are densely packed with hundreds of entries in three columns each. Full transcription requires dedicated OCR or manual effort beyond what can be done from the photographs alone. Key structural observation: signs are organized alphabetically by syllable value, with each entry giving the sign glyph, the syllable reading (underlined), and one or more manuscript reference numbers. Some entries include Tironian-system cross-references. The list also includes three whole-word sigla at the bottom of page 2: dominus, domini, domine."
  },
